message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on a children's costume set. Costumes of textile materials are classified in 9505.90 as festive articles only if they are not "wearing apparel" under the notes. Note 1(e) to Chapter 95 excludes sports clothing and fancy dress of textiles in Chapters 61 or 63. Costumes that are made up of apparel items of knit fabric, such as a dress and leggings, are therefore classified in Chapter 61. Many such rulings classify the whole set as a costume under 9505.90.6000, though this applies when the garments are flimsy and not durable, not typical apparel.

Kuromi Jester: a short sleeved pullover dress, leggings, glovelettes and a headpiece. For a set it's likely a classification as a "costume" in 9505.90.6000, since CBP often finds that costumes of flimsy construction (e.g., printed polyester knit) are festive articles. Under the Chapter 95 note, "fancy dress of textiles, of chapters 61 and 63" is excluded, but CBP has held that the "wearing apparel of textile materials" exclusion applies to garments suitable for general use. Flimsy costumes go to 9505.90.6000, which is the more likely result here.

